{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549343-pre-cast-life-protections","id":1549343,"title":"Pre-cast Life protections","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-15T11:32:27-07:00","id":1549343,"title":"Pre-cast Life protections","content":"Hello.<br /> <br /> Can I use Life 3 (or any other rank in that sphere) to protect my pattern against Life 3/4 damaging effects?<br /> <br /> Like: I met this enemy mage who wants to modify my pattern to tear me up from the inside. Could I have a pre-cast protection on me to make that (or any other similar attempt) more difficult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-15T13:42:49-07:00","id":1549344,"title":"","content":"The baseline is just giving yourself more soak/soak lethal and agg with Life 3 as a standing protection. If you have other Spheres you can have contingency healing spells on you as well (which would be a more direct 1-to-1 counter compared to extra soak, though extra soak has its own advantages).<br /> <br /> And anytime mages of the same Sphere are facing off, also means countermagic is a possibility that doesn't require any precasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-15T14:55:31-07:00","id":1549349,"title":"","content":"I dont see why not<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549343-pre-cast-life-protections?p=1549344#post1549344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The baseline is just giving yourself more soak/soak lethal and agg with Life 3 as a standing protection. If you have other Spheres you can have contingency healing spells on you as well (which would be a more direct 1-to-1 counter compared to extra soak, though extra soak has its own advantages).<br /> <br /> And anytime mages of the same Sphere are facing off, also means countermagic is a possibility that doesn't require any precasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be also my go to option. Then again i dont allow countermagic. Its no fun when 2 of 5 characters counter their solo mage enemy while the other 3 cast spells on him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-15T20:21:16-07:00","id":1549351,"title":"","content":"As a ST... I just avoid that sort of situation because the WoD action economy has long since made it necessary to account for how badly 5 vs 1 fights are completely lopsided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T04:22:49-07:00","id":1549355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549343-pre-cast-life-protections?p=1549351#post1549351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a ST... I just avoid that sort of situation because the WoD action economy has long since made it necessary to account for how badly 5 vs 1 fights are completely lopsided.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not when the mage in question attacks everyone with his aous on his turn. Then its almost even i would say. Ofc if counterspelling is banned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T09:27:21-07:00","id":1549362,"title":"","content":"An NPC mage that's powerful enough to attack every PC at once, they're powerful enough to overcome the PCs teamworking counterspells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T09:32:09-07:00","id":1549363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549343-pre-cast-life-protections?p=1549362#post1549362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An NPC mage that's powerful enough to attack every PC at once, they're powerful enough to overcome the PCs teamworking counterspells.</div> </div> </div> </div>AOE is one or 2 extra successes, when someone counterspells you you lose about 2-3 successes per counterspeller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T09:47:25-07:00","id":1549366,"title":"","content":"OK. I'm not very interested in getting into a nitpicky mechanical debate over this completely tangential point. I think you're vastly overestimating the teamwork abilities of mages, you don't. Whatever.<br /> <br /> Here's the basic point: do you want Masters than can snap their fingers and team-wipe the PCs because they have no last defense magical abilities (aka the point of counterspells), or do you want Masters that exert their power that demonstrates the decades of mastering their creativity, subtly, and their own will by using far more devastating tactics than getting into stand up fights with PCs where the PCs have the greatest advantage?<br /> <br /> I prefer such antagonists to show the intelligence to have made it as far as they have. If they were going to get shanked by a squad of weaker mages, an enemy faction would have done it already. If the PCs have done all the extra work to outmaneuver the NPC into a weak position, they deserve the tools the game gives them to benefit from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T09:51:53-07:00","id":1549367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549343-pre-cast-life-protections?p=1549366#post1549366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. I'm not very interested in getting into a nitpicky mechanical debate over this completely tangential point. I think you're vastly overestimating the teamwork abilities of mages, you don't. Whatever.<br /> <br /> Here's the basic point: do you want Masters than can snap their fingers and team-wipe the PCs because they have no last defense magical abilities (aka the point of counterspells), or do you want Masters that exert their power that demonstrates the decades of mastering their creativity, subtly, and their own will by using far more devastating tactics than getting into stand up fights with PCs where the PCs have the greatest advantage?<br /> <br /> I prefer such antagonists to show the intelligence to have made it as far as they have. If they were going to get shanked by a squad of weaker mages, an enemy faction would have done it already. If the PCs have done all the extra work to outmaneuver the NPC into a weak position, they deserve the tools the game gives them to benefit from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same can be done by just haveing defensive buffs on yourself. And it does not nagate the antagonists actions.<br /> Counterspelling is like when in a mech fight you hack the other mech making him not move. Boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 03-16-2025, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T10:15:14-07:00","id":1549369,"title":"","content":"So, as I said, you don't like the base WoD system because the action economy is actually really bad. I agree! I don't play Mage because I like how it handles things like action economy and how this impacts all sorts of things like &quot;are counterspells interesting?&quot;, I play it for other reasons and those reasons do end up with me motivating to rewrite the whole base system when I have other games I can spend far less energy working Mage-style magic into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T10:19:31-07:00","id":1549371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549343-pre-cast-life-protections?p=1549369#post1549369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as I said, you don't like the base WoD system because the action economy is actually really bad. I agree! I don't play Mage because I like how it handles things like action economy and how this impacts all sorts of things like &quot;are counterspells interesting?&quot;, I play it for other reasons and those reasons do end up with me motivating to rewrite the whole base system when I have other games I can spend far less energy working Mage-style magic into.</div> </div> </div> </div>And thats fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}